    "result_text": "The full build passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner `email` support across the OfficeFloor pipeline: present-but-valid emails are stored and returned lower-cased, invalid ones are rejected with 400, and a missing email is accepted.\n\n**Schema / DTO**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `email` string (maxLength 255) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain `email`, and MapStruct maps it both ways automatically.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the nullable `email` field with `@Column(name=\"email\")` and getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `email` column to the `owners` table.\n- `db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql` \u2014 the positional seed `INSERT`s broke with the new column, so I gave them explicit column lists (h2/postgres already used named columns).\n\n**Pipeline (per AGENTS.md conventions)**\n- New `NormalizeOwnerEmail` function \u2014 mirrors `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`: leaves a null/blank email untouched, validates a present value against a syntactic email regex, and stores the lower-cased value back on the DTO in place; throws the checked `InvalidEmailException` (\u2192 400) otherwise.\n- New `InvalidEmailException` + `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML, mirroring the telephone equivalents (400 with `{\"error\": ...}`).\n- Wired `normalizeEmail` into `owners.POST.yml` (after telephone normalization) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after validate), and updated `ApplyOwner` to copy `email` onto the entity so updates also persist the normalized value.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` (lowercasing, invalid\u2192400, missing\u21922xx) all pass, and the full suite is green.\n\nNote: I added email handling to the PUT/update endpoint too (not just the tested POST create), since the spec is phrased about owners generally \u2014 this keeps create and update consistent.",
